  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run (3 witnesses, 2 names, 3 atoms read), so I used one of the six runs.\n\n**Concept body** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/decelerating.lean`): a road user is decelerating when both of these hold:\n- its acceleration along its heading is at or below minus the deceleration tolerance;\n- it is not backing, using `drv.motion.backing` with the speed tolerance.\n\n\"At or below\" is a non-strict comparison, as the contract's words say. The body doesn't read the brake lamp or the speed. The contract fixed every choice, so I declared no narrowings.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/decelerating.lean`): one motor vehicle pointing east, observed at 0, 1 and 2 s. The instance sets the deceleration tolerance to 0.5 m/s² and the speed tolerance to 0.1 m/s.\n- **holds:** the vehicle brakes at −2 m/s² from 20 m/s while moving forward, so the result is compliant.\n- **fails:** it drives at a constant 15 m/s with zero acceleration and the brake lamp lit, so the result is violated.\n- **blind:** the holds scene with the acceleration declared absent, so the result is unknown.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
